<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">5 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 5 January, from 1066 to 1968.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-confessor" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edward-the-confessor.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1066">1066 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">960 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Edward the Confessor dies, leaving England's throne disputed</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King Edward died at Westminster without children. Rival claims by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harold-godwinson">Harold Godwinson</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harald-hardrada">Harald Hardrada</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William of Normandy</a> led to two invasions and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norman-conquest">Norman Conquest</a> that autumn.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1477">1477 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">549 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles the Bold of Burgundy killed at the Battle of Nancy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bold">Charles the Bold</a> died fighting Swiss and Lorrainer troops outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nancy">Nancy</a>. His death ended Burgundian ambitions to become a kingdom, and his lands were divided between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1757">1757 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">269 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Robert-François Damiens attempts to assassinate Louis XV</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a>, Damiens stabbed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xv">Louis XV</a> with a penknife, causing only a slight wound. He was later executed with notorious cruelty, the last person in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> to be put to death by quartering.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1919">1919 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">107 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">German Workers' Party founded in Munich</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Railway locksmith Anton Drexler founded the small nationalist German Workers' Party. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a> joined that autumn and in 1920 the party was renamed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazi-party">National Socialist German Workers' Party</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1933">1933 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">93 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Construction of the Golden Gate Bridge begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Work began on a bridge across the Golden Gate strait at the entrance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-francisco">San Francisco</a> Bay. Opened in 1937, its 1,280-metre main span was the longest in the world until 1964.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1968">1968 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexander Dubček takes charge in Czechoslovakia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Dubček replaced Antonín Novotný as leader of the Czechoslovak Communist Party. His reforms, 'socialism with a human face', inspired the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague-spring">Prague Spring</a>, ended by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw-pact">Warsaw Pact</a> invasion in August.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a></div></div></li></ol>
